Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:10:55 +0000

A pass sees trunk, its base, and the list, but the prompt only names
the base and calls upstream "trunk and mail". Nothing tells the agent
that the three differ in how settled they are, so it may ignore list
patches it could build on, or lean on a b/dev commit or list patch as
if it were final.

Describe each source and how far to trust it, so the agent consults
all three but builds a series that does not depend on the less
settled ones.
